    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In the 5-class MVP setting (Walking, Jogging, Stairs, Sitting, Standing) using accelerometer-only data and a subject-independent split, the model achieved ~69% accuracy and ~0.67 macro-F1. Performance is strongest for jogging and static postures (sitting/standing), while walking shows low recall despite high precision. This indicates the model is conservative when predicting walking and often confuses it with similar locomotion patterns (e.g., stairs) or varies due to phone placement/orientation. This behavior is expected in real-world smartphone sensing and motivates additional orientation-invariant preprocessing (e.g., separating gravity/body acceleration) and loss functions that emphasize harder examples (e.g., focal loss) as future improvements.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cBZZMj1dIuzo"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# ✅ LLM EXPLANATION LAYER (FLAN-T5) ON TOP OF MVP CNN\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# WHAT THIS DOES:\n",
        "# - Takes one accelerometer window\n",
        "# - Gets the model prediction and confidence\n",
        "# - Computes simple interpretable stats (motion intensity + jerk)\n",
        "# - Uses FLAN-T5 to generate a short natural-language explanation\n",
        "#\n",
        "# WHY:\n",
        "# - Makes your demo more polished and \"user-friendly\"\n",
        "# - Helps explain predictions without adding extra sensors or heavy models\n",
        "# - Does NOT increase classifier accuracy, but improves interpretability/UX\n",
        "\n",
        "!pip -q install transformers sentencepiece\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM, pipeline\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# ✅ STEP 1: Load FLAN-T5 model (CPU-friendly)\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "print(\"Loading FLAN-T5...\")\n",
        "model_name = \"google/flan-t5-base\"\n",
        "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
        "flan_model = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
        "\n",
        "llm = pipeline(\n",
        "    \"text2text-generation\",\n",
        "    model=flan_model,\n",
        "    tokenizer=tokenizer,\n",
        "    max_new_tokens=120\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\"✅ FLAN-T5 loaded!\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# ✅ STEP 2: Helper functions to compute interpretable stats\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "def compute_motion_stats(window):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    window: shape (T, C)\n",
        "    Expected channels:\n",
        "      - If C==5: [ax, ay, az, acc_mag/body_mag, jerk]\n",
        "      - If C==3: [ax, ay, az] (we compute mag + jerk)\n",
        "    Returns a dictionary of interpretable numbers.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if window.shape[1] == 5:\n",
        "        ax, ay, az = window[:,0], window[:,1], window[:,2]\n",
        "        mag = window[:,3]       # could be acc_mag or body_mag depending on your pipeline\n",
        "        jerk = window[:,4]\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        ax, ay, az = window[:,0], window[:,1], window[:,2]\n",
        "        mag = np.sqrt(ax*ax + ay*ay + az*az)\n",
        "        jerk = np.diff(mag, prepend=mag[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "    stats = {\n",
        "        \"mag_mean\": float(np.mean(mag)),\n",
        "        \"mag_std\":  float(np.std(mag)),\n",
        "        \"jerk_mean\": float(np.mean(np.abs(jerk))),\n",
        "        \"jerk_std\":  float(np.std(jerk)),\n",
        "        \"ax_std\": float(np.std(ax)),\n",
        "        \"ay_std\": float(np.std(ay)),\n",
        "        \"az_std\": float(np.std(az)),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    return stats\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_explanation_prompt(pred_label, confidence, stats):\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    Build a controlled prompt so the LLM stays short and safe.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
        "You are assisting a smartphone activity recognition app.\n",
        "Explain the predicted activity using ONLY the model confidence and sensor statistics below.\n",
        "\n",
        "Rules:\n",
        "- 2 to 4 short sentences.\n",
        "- Mention confidence.\n",
        "- If confidence < 0.60, say the model is uncertain and phone placement can affect readings.\n",
        "- Do NOT make medical claims or diagnosis.\n",
        "- End with one short practical tip.\n",
        "\n",
        "Prediction:\n",
        "- Activity: {pred_label}\n",
        "- Confidence: {confidence:.2f}\n",
        "\n",
        "Sensor statistics (from this window):\n",
        "- motion_mean: {stats[\"mag_mean\"]:.3f}\n",
        "- motion_std: {stats[\"mag_std\"]:.3f}\n",
        "- jerk_mean: {stats[\"jerk_mean\"]:.3f}\n",
        "- jerk_std: {stats[\"jerk_std\"]:.3f}\n",
        "- axis_std (x,y,z): {stats[\"ax_std\"]:.3f}, {stats[\"ay_std\"]:.3f}, {stats[\"az_std\"]:.3f}\n",
        "\n",
        "Now write the explanation:\n",
        "\"\"\".strip()\n",
        "    return prompt\n",
        "\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# ✅ STEP 3: Run ONE demo prediction + explanation\n",
        "# ============================================================\n",
        "# Pick a sample index from test set\n",
        "idx = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "# Get one normalized test window\n",
        "x = X_test_n[idx:idx+1]  # shape (1, T, C)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Run model prediction\n",
        "probs = model.predict(x, verbose=0)[0]\n",
        "pred_id = int(np.argmax(probs))\n",
        "confidence = float(np.max(probs))\n",
        "\n",
        "pred_label = id2cls[pred_id]\n",
        "true_label = y_test[idx]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Compute stats from the same window\n",
        "stats = compute_motion_stats(x[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "# Build prompt and generate explanation\n",
        "prompt = build_explanation_prompt(pred_label, confidence, stats)\n",
        "explanation = llm(prompt)[0][\"generated_text\"].strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n==============================\")\n",
        "print(\"✅ DEMO: Prediction + LLM Explanation\")\n",
        "print(\"==============================\")\n",
        "print(\"True label      :\", true_label)\n",
        "print(\"Predicted label :\", pred_label)\n",
        "print(\"Confidence      :\", round(confidence, 3))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n--- Motion stats ---\")\n",
        "for k,v in stats.items():\n",
        "    print(f\"{k}: {v:.4f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\n--- FLAN-T5 Explanation ---\")\n",
        "print(explanation)\n"
      ],
